{"title":"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(mass_points)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (mass points)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(quick_Menelaus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (quick Menelaus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Visual)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Visual)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Cheese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Cheese)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9_(Menelaus_+_Ceva&#39;s_+_Angle_Bisector_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9 (Menelaus + Ceva's + Angle Bisector Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Solution_10_(Menelaus_+_ABT)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 10 (Menelaus + ABT)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/5/775555f62256a77b1244bfe91ea5b61c033bb476.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=20$\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/316c50d06b5e472b3c13085b4e6285eb2e224811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />. The angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8068607716f3c2549af1dc978d77a422ca7201dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. The ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d13fd509f3062449aaea6e10e1040b1d585063f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524d9b869d9ee2d8b923afa9ce7c2c36bd9489e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7abafb670ee1184b15212c26ace11aa21637220.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = linewidth(0.7);  pair A = (0,0), C= (11,0), B=IP(CR(A,20),CR(C,18)), D = IP(B--C,CR(B,20/31*abs(B-C))), M = (A+D)/2, P = IP(M--2*M-B, A--C), D2 = IP(D--D+P-B, A--C);  D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,D(A))--MP(&quot;B&quot;,D(B),N)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,D(C))--cycle); D(A--MP(&quot;D&quot;,D(D),NE)--MP(&quot;D&#39;&quot;,D(D2))); D(B--MP(&quot;P&quot;,D(P))); D(MP(&quot;M&quot;,M,NW)); MP(&quot;20&quot;,(B+D)/2,ENE); MP(&quot;11&quot;,(C+D)/2,ENE);  [/asy]\" width=\"162\" height=\"252\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/3/b239e47c75fa1adfb0e7d7fb6bf219fcc53f86d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/632d6d77169ce71d5d876d8da869f89ebfc87b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP \\parallel DD&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"19\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915e5b1d2f06b6555ecf6b6ea910ccff1a0f7af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC \\sim \\triangle DD&#39;C$\" width=\"149\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d05af9a5c0a321353aeb939daa73c831db323e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{PC}{D&#39;C} = 1 + \\frac{BD}{DC} = 1 + \\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{31}{11}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"38\" /> by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>. Similarly, we see by the Midline Theorem that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d4698a68bf6d67b0e77d7b8560b33bd9f18b6bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = PD&#39;$\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30ac56058a004898d146cc3899e0f98ffe87df2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{CP}{PA} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{PD&#39;}{PC}} = \\frac{1}{1 - \\frac{D&#39;C}{PC}} = \\frac{31}{20},\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"44\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4edec466070c5b894fa456a878f15c4107f3be7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28mass_points.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(mass_points)\">Solution 2 (mass points)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (mass points)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assign <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mass_points\" title=\"Mass points\">mass points</a> as follows: by Angle-Bisector Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba35fc9c72243cb03aa4ea387d955956cc3f5952.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD / DC = 20/11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />, so we assign <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/8/9c8b2396cdced5a78c2bdb9d3020d5dd9c2f4bac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(B) = 11, m(C) = 20, m(D) = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"277\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/22868ed6f19158516a44f9a593267ccd97a4e785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = MD$\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b4b3156b28cf607d35b4fe76ab103be1785d9f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(A) = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/9129f0a8cfbd99ec11510bf16dad0ce669af52bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CP}{PA} = \\frac{m(A) }{ m(C)} = \\frac{31}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"150\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4edec466070c5b894fa456a878f15c4107f3be7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Menelaus%27_Theorem\" title=\"Menelaus&#39; Theorem\">Menelaus' Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Transversal\" title=\"Transversal\">transversal</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa8a05c156abc5702313c8aade15cfe46e1aec3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = \\frac{CP}{PA} \\cdot \\frac{AM}{MD} \\cdot \\frac{DB}{CB} = \\frac{CP}{PA} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{AC}{AB}}\\right) \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\frac{CP}{PA} = \\frac{31}{20}.\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"53\" /> So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/9/d095633acc5182d182a71c8abbc52adc716587b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{051}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will use barycentric coordinates. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5594734f575ba9bb2b41af9aebde75dcddb18834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (1, 0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4ef78f5ccf5a4501c80d01c6131c71361ef7a553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (0, 1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2fd56e5e6cc30249cdd51c3121d4622fdbc53a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = (0, 0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f9055a4a2b0ad190800b8e8f4761d0d593bda5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = [0:11:20] = \\left(0, \\frac{11}{31}, \\frac{20}{31}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"247\" height=\"45\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776e68c53c39754b7cbe4058f3ad985cd54cefd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\frac{A + D}{2} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{11}{62}, \\frac{10}{31}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"219\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore, the equation for line BM is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8ff524d579b051814dd7ce2a87879d8b05e4175.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20x = 31z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95ba34514329976518d3af67b22252b2097edeeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = (x, 0, 1-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />. Using the equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8068607716f3c2549af1dc978d77a422ca7201dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec3fcc57040af416bd4292779beaebc51253051.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[20x = 31(1-x)\\]\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06d0580c2da3fee119cdd22d56960a2b90143db6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{31}{51}\\]\" width=\"54\" height=\"38\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34a3c212b1f5303abd44b7e8392415e8830e64f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CP}{PA} = \\frac{1-x}{x} = \\frac{31}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"37\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7324b643e2152af545afd49d89d40b74e8308436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{051}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/5/ea5427920c3bbf4c4c5e4e00ea94265381c157b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=x$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. Then by the Angle Bisector Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/a/8ca7ed2187e8c3f8c4e3ea8855fd78b3faca00ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=\\frac{20}{11}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />. By the Ratio Lemma, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d44cb15b71ebcfc134947a58a885b1a4ea1e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PC}{AP}=\\frac{\\frac{31}{11}x\\sin\\angle PBC}{20\\sin\\angle ABP}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"176\" height=\"40\" /> Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a190b864c0b419f8aae38368ba08bdf62aa73a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle BAM]=[\\triangle BMD]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" /> since their bases have the same length and they share a height. By the sin area formula, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06a492ff278324ad51946cc3055c2f3d4e76aeb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot20\\cdot BM\\cdot \\sin\\angle ABP=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{20}{11}x\\cdot BM\\cdot\\sin\\angle PBC.\\]\" width=\"411\" height=\"37\" /> Simplifying, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/e/ade0bee343aa3a5eaeb45895e00027a4ee0e6ac3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin\\angle PBC}{\\sin\\angle ABP}=\\frac{11}{x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"39\" /> Plugging this into what we got from the Ratio Lemma, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14cfa0f52f6828e5e9bd2b4e85ec8044b018937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PC}{AP}=\\frac{31}{20}\\implies\\boxed{051.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"172\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28quick_Menelaus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(quick_Menelaus)\">Solution 6 (quick Menelaus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (quick Menelaus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we will find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4af53e8c42e7fd9156766800dd21ab7cf508f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{MP}{BP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"36\" height=\"37\" />. By Menelaus on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/adabea46b0d9b36b24726918eaa7933e1cb16433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e09ea5a025ef40715a73b55803de1091a920e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BC}{CD}\\cdot\\frac{DA}{AM}\\cdot\\frac{MP}{PB}=1\\implies \\frac{62MP}{11BP}=1\\implies \\frac{MP}{BP}=\\frac{11}{62}.\\]\" width=\"442\" height=\"38\" />\nThis implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce474c7a4de164b6a410012c9f4774880b96fbef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{MB}{BP}=1-\\frac{MP}{BP}=\\frac{51}{62}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"176\" height=\"37\" />. Then, by Menelaus on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322ef01b220105183559cbefe52c6852abe9a0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AMP$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51acc690386a32186c76703761ed256839d1231b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AD}{DM}\\cdot\\frac{MB}{BP}\\cdot\\frac{PC}{CA}=1\\implies \\frac{PC}{CA}=\\frac{31}{51}.\\]\" width=\"299\" height=\"38\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de13249f4483f885b3af3db34f25331bd4061db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PC}{AP}=\\frac{31}{51-31}=\\frac{31}{20}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" /> The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7324b643e2152af545afd49d89d40b74e8308436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{051}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. -brainiacmaniac31\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Visual.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Visual)\">Solution 7 (Visual)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Visual)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2011_AIME_II_4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/c1/2011_AIME_II_4.png/400px-2011_AIME_II_4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"411\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/c1/2011_AIME_II_4.png 1.5x\" /></a></span>\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Cheese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Cheese)\">Solution 8 (Cheese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Cheese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a right triangle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc975a5b35343ca18565b3a7cce9827d332bbbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = x$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca35b46a5e25dde214d715f41dac1253472f7c5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = \\tfrac{-11}{20}x + 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />. These two lines intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> which have coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/98789f345677a9bf99b98bb06f76e0c8ce6215b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{220}{31},\\frac{220}{31})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/2/5121ee8b42777c01db03461033702fd216a7063b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{110}{31},\\frac{110}{31})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d48f7980036da82f5f438c4acb29ee54a178c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM = \\tfrac{11}{51} \\cdot (20-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"156\" height=\"23\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> coordinate equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/1/7218a0e6fb58487c3a20d7e04b6e68a8d6846c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11\\cdot20}{51} \\frac{AP + CP}{AP} = 1 + \\frac{CP}{AP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"226\" height=\"39\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d31f48e67dc2b76bbf0dfa26bfa9c9005790fce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{51}{20} = 1 + \\frac{CP}{AP},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"112\" height=\"39\" /> which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111fa6e10767e6b425584220935aa12082e4623a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\tfrac{31}{20}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" /> giving an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee51821c932a5c7288419b3af02c42086329cc4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{51}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"36\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_9_.28Menelaus_.2B_Ceva.27s_.2B_Angle_Bisector_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9_(Menelaus_+_Ceva's_+_Angle_Bisector_Theorem)\">Solution 9 (Menelaus + Ceva's + Angle Bisector Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9 (Menelaus + Ceva&#39;s + Angle Bisector Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start by using Menelaus' theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a771251838750a4cb9926c5e2b03324b2b2edae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\nSo, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/1/4a1972946cd07e3129ec2c121dfb605111a1af8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC}{DC}\\cdot\\frac{DM}{AM}\\cdot\\frac{AE}{EB}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"168\" height=\"39\" />.\nBy Angle Bisector theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b41c0295b2d98e631e865292ab42b9d7ac171e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC}{DC}=\\frac{31}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"39\" />, and therefore after plugging in our values we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c719b77ae16f1f75cb67eceaf2df2a02fcfccdc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AE}{EB}=\\frac{11}{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" />.\nThen, by Ceva's on the whole figure, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17def61029b73ebbc312c846b8376ba7fa8cd8c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CP}{PA}\\cdot\\frac{AE}{EB}\\cdot\\frac{BD}{DC}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"161\" height=\"39\" />.\nPlugging in our values, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/0448210594118adf690e06a0e82fa9a3234b02cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CP}{PA}=\\frac{31}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" />, giving an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d295acf5c767958d7fb6b98f637296221dce16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{51}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n~ESAOPS\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_10_.28Menelaus_.2B_ABT.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_10_(Menelaus_+_ABT)\">Solution 10 (Menelaus + ABT)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 10 (Menelaus + ABT)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Menelaus' theorem w.r.t <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and transversal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4bb1db3d066da48df7576e30ef3831ec64cecc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BP}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4080618166fa6e170d2496fc096c97352a83af59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PA}{CP}\\cdot\\frac{BC}{BD}\\cdot\\frac{DM}{AM}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"167\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12b6767375342ed57d27678e3ea1cdb97f47e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a878c75ae187f6129d4b5de7e75c2ffd8a1222f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PA}{CP}\\cdot\\frac{BC}{BD} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Now, we chase the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/976cceed20ca47cb88a27a60bd3a6ff95b7bc7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC}{BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"36\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>By the Angle bisector theorem w.r.t <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83302ccbe917a7af6bb355893e545b734557924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AC}{CD} = \\frac{AB}{BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12b6767375342ed57d27678e3ea1cdb97f47e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f2ec732b6ff9d50970e0dfc993654742834148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{BD} = \\frac{11}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12b6767375342ed57d27678e3ea1cdb97f47e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbebfae384ecf02b97a5c1594d077496b2304baa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC}{BD} = \\frac{31}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>So, from our Menelaus' equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd872f83854e74f154a1dfb01adc4635b00f8a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PA}{CP} = \\frac{20}{31}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e12b6767375342ed57d27678e3ea1cdb97f47e15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9550a122bb563c1cd54a189123bb4aba60817c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n = 20 + 31 = \\boxed{051}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"197\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~cheltstudent\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Gjt25jRiFns?t=314\">https://youtu.be/Gjt25jRiFns?t=314</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II\" title=\"2011 AIME II\">2011 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">